  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5415",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N is implicated in the pathogenesis of SW780 through multiple, interconnected mechanisms. The evidence suggests that Mollicellin N acts as a target for several receptors, including P2X purinoceptors 1 and 7, which are known to mediate cellular signaling pathways involved in inflammation and cell survival. These receptors are further targeted by a common compound, [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate, which has a known effect on SW780. This compound is also a target of palmarumycin CP18, which is itself a known inhibitor of SW780. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Mollicellin N in modulating cellular responses through these receptors, possibly influencing SW780's viability or function. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Mollicellin N and SW780, particularly through the activation of P2X receptors and their downstream signaling, which may contribute to the observed effects on the cell line.",
